tten in the  past about Donald Trump's finances the  documents were the first page  of a New York State resident income tax  return the first page of a New Jersey  non-resident tax return and the first  page of a Connecticut non-resident  return each page contained the social  security number of both Donald Trump and  his then wife Marla maples now the three  documents showed up at the New York  Times by mail with a postmark indicating  that they were sent from within New York  City the return address claimed that the  documents came from Trump Tower now of  course you can write any return address  and then just drop it in a New York City  mailbox and it will be postmarked in New  York City and it will have whatever  return address you wrote on it let's  keep that in mind the New York Times  took these documents and presented them  to Jack Mitnick who's a lawyer and  certified public accountant who actually  handled Donald Trump's tax returns for  more than 30 years until 1996 mr.  Mitnick was listed on this New Jersey  tax form as the preparer he's now  semi-retired and living in Florida said  he no longer has access to Donald  Trump's tax returns but that indeed the  documents appear to be authentic parts  of Donald Trump's tax returns and that  the signature purportedly on these  documents is indeed his okay so let's  take a look at a couple things here  first and foremost I want to show you  the bit of Donald Trump's tax returns  where we see a nine hundred and fifteen  point seven million dollar negative  adjusted gross income okay we can't say  for sure the implications of this loss  on future years because we don't have  Donald Trump's tax returns for future  years but we do know that a loss this  big in 1995 would have been large enough  to wipe out 50 million dollars per year  of taxable income over the following 18  years  Donald Trump has declined to comment on  the documents instead the campaign put  out a statement that it doesn't chow  nor confirmed th