nd see that he was a good  businessman he was legitimately  successful in business I I don't agree  with the way that Mitt Romney took  advantage of taking businesses apart and  hurting many employees I don't agree  with the model personally on a moral  level but it was verifiable we of course  have no reason to believe that good  business people make good presidents and  that remains with both Trump and Mitt  Romney but Mitt Romney's narrative was  at least verifiable and true this is a  potential disaster for Donald Trump on  many levels Hillary Clinton appears to  have been right that's number one  Donald Trump every indication is he's  hiding something terrible in his tax  returns  number two Donald Trump's businessman  credentials are also called into  question losing a billion dollars in a  year could be some kind of tax strategy  right he might have paid in a billion  dollars of his personal wealth into his  businesses allowing him to show a  billion dollar loss and then in  subsequent years being able to use that  loss to offset taxes on future income  that's one possibility and it would be  legal but incredibly manipulative and  really I would argue completely  unpatriotic or it could be that he's not  as good of a businessman as he claims  and this billion dollar loss in a year  was the result of bad business decisions  either case is not particularly good for  Donald Trump the broader analysis is  everyday this is in the the news it is  not good for Donald Trump and my  prediction is we will be hearing more  about this there will be more  information surfacing I was recently  sent and I've been wearing a really cool  watch from movement watches also known  as MVM tea and I absolutely love this  watch a lot of people have been asking  me about it movement watches is  interesting because they started  similarly to how the david pakman show  started which was it was two broke  college kids who wanted to wear stylish  watches but couldn't afford them so they 